					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/castchaos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1389813); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1389813&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607936197" alt="CastChaos" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1389813)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/castchaos" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1389813); return false;" >CastChaos</a></span> <span class="odate time_1346844850 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">05 Sep 2012 11:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1556616">
									

<p>Beyond the clichés, this doesn't do too many interesting things anyway. I almost started to get interested when the containment breach broadcast started, but it let me down that it was just one, and it kept repeating the same thing over and over. At least the description could have mentioned more examples of what was broadcasted so far&#8230; it still would be like the tome that describes alternate events when the Foundation messes things up and the world ends, but this one could describe them in news format and mention the events in detail.<br />
And that radiation thing seems like an invidual addition that is there just to be there, or maybe to avoid &quot;deletion because too few and cliché anomalies&quot;, it could at least be tied to the broadcasts in any way, like, the more grim the news are, the heavier the radiation&#8230;<br />
Plus we already have a TV that knows about the Foundation in detail, it makes the show &quot;Cash or Ash&quot;. And this TV is old AGAIN. Like most/kinda all other tv SCPs.</p>
<p>No vote so far, but as I write this comment, it starts to feel more and more as an intentional cliché collection&#8230;</p>

